 file-findings [N]\n    attavo file-stops [N]\n    attavo counsel [N]\n    attavo record-only\n    attavo attest [--partial] [N]\n    attavo drive [N] [--until-ready | --report]\n    attavo ledger [N] [--json]\n    attavo stops [N] [--json]\n\nThe doctor is the definition of done. It asserts five proofs against a\ntenant root and exits 1 until every proof holds:\n\n  1. every-gate-rejects      every gate in the manifest's [gates] table,\n                             run against its rejection fixture, exits non-zero,\n                             and carries a non-empty retires\n  2. one-item-every-stage    one work item under paths.records carries a\n                             record for every stage -- spec, approval,\n                             build, verify -- all four introduced by one\n                             merge commit reachable from HEAD\n  3. no-commit-lacks-record  every commit on the default branch after the\n                             manifest was introduced is named by a record's\n                             sha or commits list, or itself writes under\n                             paths.records (a record is committed with the\n                             code it describes; an item's merge commit\n                             carries its own record paths this way)\n  4. no-stop-lacks-cause     every build or verify record under\n                             paths.records at record_version 3 or later,\n                             with a status other than pass, carries a stop\n                             naming an enumerated class and provenance, a\n                             non-empty detail when unclassed, the gates\n                             heading when a build failed after running\n                             them, and the tool's own error line when an\n                             adapter exit ended the log -- records before\n                             record_version 3 are counted and reported,\n                             never refused\n  5. every-attested-item-is-sealed\n                             every merged item that carries a record for\n                             every stage has a statement in the forge's\n                             attestation store for its merge commit, read\n                             through [forge].attestation_command -- a\n                             merge at or before [forge].sealed_since is\n                             named as before the window instead of failed.\n\"\"\"bin/attavo --help and its unknown-subcommand message name every\nsubcommand that exists, and the product itself names no vendor. Issue\n#54, acceptance 10 and 11.\n\nRun: python3 -m pytest tests -q\n\"\"\"\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nATTAVO = ROOT / \"bin\" / \"attavo\"\n\n\ndef test_help_lists_attest_and_record_only() -> None:\n    run = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(ATTAVO), \"--help\"],\n                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    assert run.returncode == 0\n    assert \"attavo record-only\" in run.stdout\n    assert \"attavo attest\" in run.stdout\n\n\ndef test_help_names_all_four_doctor_proofs() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Issue #94, acceptance row 5: the doctor's own help text names all\n    four proofs, no-stop-lacks-cause included -- a proof the help text\n    forgets is one a reader would never know to expect from doctor: done.\"\"\"\n    run = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(ATTAVO), \"--help\"],\n                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    assert run.returncode == 0\n    assert \"every-gate-rejects\" in run.stdout\n    assert \"one-item-every-stage\" in run.stdout\n    assert \"no-commit-lacks-record\" in run.stdout\n    assert \"no-stop-lacks-cause\" in run.stdout\n\n\ndef test_help_names_the_drive_report_and_the_states_it_prints() -> None:\n    run = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(ATTAVO), \"--help\"],\n                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    assert run.returncode == 0\n    assert \"attavo drive [N] [--until-ready | --report]\" in run.stdout\n    assert \"schema/drive-report.schema.json\" in run.stdout\n    assert \"(yours, waits, acts, done)\" in \" \".join(run.stdout.split())\n\n\ndef test_unknown_subcommand_message_names_attest_and_record_only() -> None:\n    run = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(ATTAVO), \"not-a-real-subcommand\"],\n                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n    assert run.returncode == 2\n    assert \"record-only\" in run.stderr\n    assert \"attest\" in run.stderr\n\n\ndef test_no_vendor_name_in_bin_attavo() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Acceptance 11. The four pre-existing code-factory hits this check\n    once had to carve out lived in test docstrings, not in bin/attavo\n    itself; this check's own scope is bin/attavo alone, so it stays a\n    plain empty-output assertion.\"\"\"\n    run = subprocess.run(\n        [\"git\", \"grep\", \"-n\", \"-i\", \"-E\", \"github|sigstore|in-toto\", \"--\", \"bin/attavo\"],\n        cwd=str(ROOT), capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\nattavo.toml:7:checks_command = \"python3 .attavo/bin/forge-checks\"\ntests/conftest.py:11:    \"\"\"The drive's forge poll reads its bound and interval from the environment at call time (issue #84) so a test never waits out the production bound; since #178 verify polls too, and a fixture whose checks_command prints nothing is unconcluded and would wait 600 s. Every test gets a sub-second clock unless it sets its own.\"\"\"\ntests/test_executor_conformance.py:99:    env.pop(\"ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND\", None)\ntests/test_executor_conformance.py:253:def test_situation_7_the_one_test_command_in_the_invocation(adapter_name: str, tmp_path: Path) -> None:\ntests/test_executor_conformance.py:263:        \"ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND\": checks})\ntests/test_testtool.py:161:def test_build_hands_the_executor_the_test_command_and_no_checks_comman