{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HyEgAVZF5ZrQoedxWwVzuB","type":"tool_result","content":"# Adapters\n\nAn adapter is an executable at `adapters/<name>/run`, resolved first under\nthe tenant's `attavo/adapters/`, then under this product's `adapters/`.\n`attavo build` invokes it with the tenant root as its working directory.\n\n## Environment\n\n- `ATTAVO_SPEC_DIR` — the work item's spec directory (`spec.md`, `criteria/`, `stub/`).\n- `ATTAVO_RECORDS_DIR` — the work item's own records directory.\n- `ATTAVO_RULINGS` — the tenant's rulings file (`paths.rulings`).\n- `ATTAVO_BRANCH` — the branch the adapter must commit on.\n- `ATTAVO_ITERATION` — the 1-based attempt number within this `attavo build` invocation.\n- `ATTAVO_FEEDBACK` — a file holding the previous iteration's failing criteria, test output, and checks output; empty on the first iteration.\n- `ATTAVO_ADAPTER_CONFIG` — the tenant manifest's `[executor.<adapter-name>]` table, serialized as JSON (`{}` when the tenant declared none). The product does not know what an adapter's settings mean; each adapter documents its own keys on its own `README.md`. **Never put a secret in this table** — it is copied verbatim into `build-NN.json` as `adapter_config`, and a record is not where secrets live.\n- `ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND` — the tenant's `[checks].command`, unset when the tenant declared no `[checks]` table. The product does not know what it checks; the tenant does. An adapter should tell the executor it is part of done when set, and say nothing about checks when it is not.\n- `ATTAVO_STAGE` — `\"build\"`, `\"verify\"`, or `\"counsel\"` (issue #100), which invocation this is. An adapter that supports every stage branches on it; one that only builds may ignore it.\n- `ATTAVO_EVENTS` — build and verify only: a file path an adapter may append events to while it runs (issue #26). Absent on a stage that does not set it (counsel does not); an adapter that never checks for it breaks nothing.\n- `ATTAVO_DIFF` — verify only: a file holding the diff since the build's approval.\n- `ATTAVO_BUILD_RECORD` — verify only: the path to the `build-NN.json` being verified.\n- `ATTAVO_COUNSEL_RECORD` — counsel only: the path to the non-pass `build-NN.json`/`verify-NN.json` being counseled.\n- `ATTAVO_COUNSEL_LOG` — counsel only: the path to that record's own `.log`, empty when it has none.\n- `ATTAVO_COUNSEL_DIFF` — counsel only: a file holding the item's diff since approval (the same diff verify itself would compute).\n- `ATTAVO_MANIFEST` — counsel only: the path to the tenant's own `attavo.toml`.\n- `ATTAVO_PRODUCT_ROOT` — counsel only: the path to this product's own root (`bin/attavo`, `adapters/`, `schema/`, `templates/`), so a stop whose cause is the product's own mechanism can be read at it.\n- `GIT_AUTHOR_NAME`, `GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL`, `GIT_COMMITTER_NAME`, `GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL` — build only: the executor's identity (issue #33), set by the product and never the tenant's git config. An adapter must not override these for the commits it makes; a commit build finds not carrying this identity is refused.\n\n### The executor sees none of it (issue #198)\n\nThe variables above are the adapter's contract, not the executor's. An\nadapter launches its executor with every `ATTAVO_*` name removed from the\nchild's environment and keeps reading its own. The executor's tools would\notherwise inherit `ATTAVO_EVENTS`, the item's live events file, and write\nto it: a test suite the executor runs that runs `adapters/fixture/run`\nappended 26 of 83 lines to one item's events file (attavo/attavo#194,\nbuild-01). The adapters here pass `executor_env()` from\n`adapters/executor_env.py` as `env=` to the process that runs the\nexecutor; a tenant's own adapter does the same, by that helper's rule\n(drop every name starting `ATTAVO_`, keep the rest). Situations 20 and 21\nof `tests/test_executor_conformance.py` check it through the tool binary\n\n- `auth` — `\"api\"` (default) or `\"subscription\"`.\n  - `\"api\"`: runs with `--bare`. Requires `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`; usage bills per token.\n  - `\"subscription\"`: omits `--bare`; adds `--setting-sources user` and `--strict-mcp-config` so the tenant's project hooks and MCP servers do not load (`CLAUDE.md` still does). Runs on the operator's subscription login; usage is included in the plan. `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is not required.\n- `model` — omitted means the executor's default. When set, passed as `--model`, and trusted verbatim as the record's `model` rather than picked out of the tool's own usage report (issue #77).\n- `setting_sources` — default `\"user\"`. Only meaningful in subscription mode; ignored in api mode (`--bare` already excludes everything).\n- `permission_mode` — default `\"acceptEdits\"`.\n- `allowed_tools` is retired (issue #78): a manifest that still declares `[executor.claude-code].allowed_tools` is refused by name rather than silently accepted or ignored. See below.\n\n## The tenant's checks\n\n`attavo build` already runs `[checks].command` after each commit and feeds\na failure back on the next iteration — the executor is not the runner of\nthe tenant's checks. When `ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND` is set (`../README.md`),\nthe instruction says so: \"after you commit, the tenant's checks (`<command>`)\nare run for you and any failure is returned to you on the next iteration;\nrun only what you need while editing.\" When it is unset, the instruction\nsays nothing about checks.\n\n## The sandbox is the boundary, not an allowed_tools list\n\nEvery invocation carries `--settings` with a `sandbox` object\n(`sandbox.enabled: true`, `allowUnsandboxedCommands: false`,\n`network.allowedDomains: []`) — confirmed live against `claude 2.1.268`:\nthe sandbox refuses a write outside the working directory and any\noutbound connection, at the OS level, before `--allowedTools` is ever\nconsulted. Verify's `--settings` additionally sets\n`filesystem.denyWrite` on the working directory itself, so \"make no\nedits, write no files\" is mechanical rather than merely instructed.\n`--allowedTools` is therefore fixed per stage to the tool names the\nsandbox does not itself govern — `Read,Edit,Write,Bash` for build,\n47:  where `findings`/`tests_named` (verify) or `status`/`question` (build)\n63:the same shape `tests/test_adapter_codex.py`'s own recorded fixture\n130:  diagnostic with the suite's own test seams. `OPENAI_API_KEY` alone is\n131:  deterministic, fully testable, and already closes the concrete risk\n{\n  \"dry_run_env\": \"ATTAVO_ADAPTER_DRY_RUN\",\n  \"response_env\": \"ATTAVO_ADAPTER_RESPONSE_FILE\",\n  \"tool_binary\": \"claude\",\n  \"stages\": [\"build\", \"verify\", \"counsel\"],\n  \"reports\": [\"tokens\", \"cost_usd\"],\n  \"input_limit\": {\n    \"unit\": null,\n    \"value\": null,\n    \"reason\": \"claude code documents no numeric input-size ceiling anywhere in its own surface (--help, docs, or any config file, confirmed against claude 2.1.269) -- this adapter asserts its own instruction stays under a fixed 64 KB bound instead\"\n  },\n  \"success_script\": \"#!/bin/sh\\ngit commit -q --allow-empty -m 'adapter commit'\\nprintf '{\\\"type\\\": \\\"result\\\", \\\"is_error\\\": false, \\\"structured_output\\\": {\\\"status\\\": \\\"done\\\", \\\"question\\\": null}, \\\"usage\\\": {\\\"input_tokens\\\": 1, \\\"output_tokens\\\": 1}, \\\"modelUsage\\\": {\\\"claude-sonnet-5\\\": {\\\"inputTokens\\\": 1, \\\"outputTokens\\\": 1}}}\\\\n'\\n\",\n  \"subagent_guard\": {\n    \"supported\": true,\n    \"situation\": \"subagent_spawned\",\n    \"note\": \"issue #88, class B -- checked against the tool's own subagent_stats.spawned, named in --disallowedTools by 'Agent' and 'Workflow' (confirmed live, claude 2.1.269, see adapters/claude-code/run's own docstring)\"\n  },\n  \"situations\": {\n    \"done\": {\n      \"is_error\": false,\n      \"structured_output\": {\"status\": \"done\", \"question\": null},\n      \"usage\": {\"input_tokens\": 5, \"output_tokens\": 9},\n      \"total_cost_usd\": 0.01,\n      \"modelUsage\": {\"claude-sonnet-5\": {\"inputTokens\": 5, \"outputTokens\": 9}}\n    },\n    \"is_error\": {\n      \"is_error\": true,\n      \"result\": \"API error: overloaded\",\n      \"structured_output\": {\"status\": \"done\", \"question\": null},\n      \"usage\": {\"input_tokens\": 1, \"output_tokens\": 1},\n      \"modelUsage\": {\"claude-sonnet-5\": {\"inputTokens\": 1, \"outputTokens\": 1}}\n    },\n    \"no_structured_output\": {\n      \"is_error\": false,\n      \"usage\": {\"input_tokens\": 1, \"output_tokens\": 1},\n      \"modelUsage\": {\"claude-sonnet-5\": {\"inputTokens\": 1, \"outputTokens\": 1}}\n    },\n    \"question_null\": {\n      \"is_error\": false,\n      \"structured_output\": {\"status\": \"question\", \"question\": null},\n27:`attavo build N` refuses (exit 1, naming the cause, no record) unless the manifest declares `[executor].build` and `[tests].select` and `[tests].run`, and unless `attavo approval-status` would print `valid`. It invokes the named adapter — `adapters/<name>/run`, resolved first under the tenant's own `attavo/adapters/`, then under this product's `adapters/` — with the spec, the corpus, and the branch. After each return it checks that every path the adapter touched matches a spec claim, then runs the criteria against the tree, the tests `[tests].select` and `[tests].run` name for the touched paths, and — when the manifest declares `[checks].command` — the tenant's own whole-tree check, from the tenant root. `pass` requires every criterion, the test run, and the tenant's checks (if declared) to exit 0; a non-zero exit anywhere iterates, with the failure as feedback, up to a fixed budget. `[checks]` is optional; a tenant that declares none is not refused, unlike `[tests]`. A `question` from the adapter halts the loop at once (exit 3); nothing answers it in Phase 2. Every run writes the next `build-NN.json`, with the adapter's transcript beside it as `build-NN.log`. Nothing dispatches build; it is typed by the operator. The full contract is in the Phase 2 issue.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8327c9db-455b-4a76-8736-ba592c30dfef","uuid":"f80614a2-f026-4dbf-b869-fb7dd3792bdb","timestamp":"2026-09-21T01:42:47.245Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Adapters\n\nAn adapter is an executable at `adapters/<name>/run`, resolved first under\nthe tenant's `attavo/adapters/`, then under this product's `adapters/`.\n`attavo build` invokes it with the tenant root as its working directory.\n\n## Environment\n\n- `ATTAVO_SPEC_DIR` — the work item's spec directory (`spec.md`, `criteria/`, `stub/`).\n- `ATTAVO_RECORDS_DIR` — the work item's own records directory.\n- `ATTAVO_RULINGS` — the tenant's rulings file (`paths.rulings`).\n- `ATTAVO_BRANCH` — the branch the adapter must commit on.\n- `ATTAVO_ITERATION` — the 1-based attempt number within this `attavo build` invocation.\n- `ATTAVO_FEEDBACK` — a file holding the previous iteration's failing criteria, test output, and checks output; empty on the first iteration.\n- `ATTAVO_ADAPTER_CONFIG` — the tenant manifest's `[executor.<adapter-name>]` table, serialized as JSON (`{}` when the tenant declared none). The product does not know what an adapter's settings mean; each adapter documents its own keys on its own `README.md`. **Never put a secret in this table** — it is copied verbatim into `build-NN.json` as `adapter_config`, and a record is not where secrets live.\n- `ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND` — the tenant's `[checks].command`, unset when the tenant declared no `[checks]` table. The product does not know what it checks; the tenant does. An adapter should tell the executor it is part of done when set, and say nothing about checks when it is not.\n- `ATTAVO_STAGE` — `\"build\"`, `\"verify\"`, or `\"counsel\"` (issue #100), which invocation this is. An adapter that supports every stage branches on it; one that only builds may ignore it.\n- `ATTAVO_EVENTS` — build and v