{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BRYh7FSXzBZF1A3ki9WqLv","type":"tool_result","content":"spec-gate, approve, and approval-status are gates and writers. They run\nfrom the tenant root (the current working directory); N, the work item id,\nis read from the ATTAVO_ITEM environment variable when set, else from the\nbranch (attavo/N-*). The doctor's first proof sets ATTAVO_ITEM for a\nrejection fixture's own item, so a gate's own command needs no argument\neven while the enclosing repository sits on a real item's attavo/N-*\nbranch. Every run of spec-gate or approve writes the next numbered attempt\nfile under paths.records/N/ and never overwrites one already written. See\nthe spec contract in the project's Phase 1 issue for the full rules each\none enforces.\n\nbuild refuses (exit 1, naming the cause, no record) unless the manifest\ndeclares [executor].build and [tests].select and [tests].run, and unless\napproval-status would print valid. It exports the executor's identity\n(issue #33) into the adapter's environment as GIT_AUTHOR_NAME/EMAIL and\nGIT_COMMITTER_NAME/EMAIL, set by the product and never the tenant's git\nconfig, then invokes the named adapter (adapters/<name>/run) with the\nspec, the corpus, and the branch. It refuses (status refused) a commit\nbetween start_sha and HEAD not authored by that identity, checks that\nevery path touched matches a spec claim, records the adapter's own\ndeclared \"reports\" -- the fields adapters/<name>/conformance.json says\nit can supply with a real value (issue #41), so a field it claims and\nnever supplies is a defect the conformance suite catches rather than a\nsilent null -- then runs the criteria, the\ntests [tests].select and [tests].run name for the touched paths, and --\nwhen the manifest declares [checks].command -- the tenant's own\nwhole-tree check, from the tenant root. pass requires every criterion,\nthe test run, and the tenant's checks (if declared) to exit 0; any\nnon-zero exit iterates, with the failure as feedback, up to a fixed\nbudget. [checks] is optional; a tenant that declares none is not\nrefused. It writes the next build-NN.json under paths.records/N/, with\nthe adapter's transcript -- each iteration's gate output (criteria\nexits, the selected tests' stdout, the tenant's checks' tail) appended\nunder an \"--- attavo gates, iteration N ---\" heading, issue #89 -- beside\nit as build-NN.log. Every record whose status is not pass carries stop:\n{class, provenance, detail}, derived from the refusal, halted, and log\nalready on hand (issue #89); a pass record carries stop: null. See the","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8327c9db-455b-4a76-8736-ba592c30dfef","uuid":"81ce8fd9-33ed-4e23-aa1d-270d1d393c8b","timestamp":"2026-09-21T01:46:42.215Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"spec-gate, approve, and approval-status are gates and writers. They run\nfrom the tenant root (the current working directory); N, the work item id,\nis read from the ATTAVO_ITEM environment variable when set, else from the\nbranch (attavo/N-*). The doctor's first proof sets ATTAVO_ITEM for a\nrejection fixture's own item, so a gate's own command needs no argument\neven while the enclosing repository sits on a real item's attavo/N-*\nbranch. Every run of spec-gate or approve writes the next numbered attempt\nfile under paths.records/N/ and never overwrites one already written. See\nthe spec contract in the project's Phase 1 issue for the full rules each\none enforces.\n\nbuild refuses (exit 1, naming the cause, no record) unless the manifest\ndeclares [executor].build and [tests].select and [tests].run, and unless\napproval-status would print valid. It exports the executor's identity\n(issue #33) into the adapter's environment as GIT_AUTHOR_NAME/EMAIL and\nGIT_COMMITTER_NAME/EMAIL, set by the product and never the tenant's git\nconfig, then invokes the named adapter (adapters/<name>/run) with the\nspec, the corpus, and the branch. It refuses (status refused) a commit\nbetween start_sha and HEAD not authored by that identity, checks that\nevery path touched matches a spec claim, records the adapter's own\ndeclared \"reports\" -- the fields adapters/<name>/conformance.json says\nit can supply with a real value (issue #41), so a field it claims and\nnever supplies is a defect the conformance suite catches rather than a\nsilent null -- then runs the criteria, the\ntests [tests].select and [tests].run name for the touched paths, and --\nwhen the manifest declares [checks].command -- the tenant's own\nwhole-tree check, from the tenant root. pass requires every criterion,\nthe test run, and the tenant's checks (if declared) to exit 0; any\nnon-zero exit iterates, with the failure as feedback, up to a fixed\nbudget. [checks] is optional; a tenant that declares none is not\nrefused. It writes the next build-NN.json under paths.records/N/, with\nthe adapter's transcript -- each iteration's gate output (criteria\nexits, the selected tests' stdout, the tenant's checks' tail) appended\nunder an \"--- attavo gates, iteration N ---\" heading, issue #89 -- beside\nit as build-NN.log. Every record whose status is not pass carries stop:\n{class, provenance, detail}, derived from the refusal, halted, and log\nalready on hand (issue #89); a pass record carries stop: null. See the","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfFjvvRVAsJwfQvDJVsCx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TYDQtfnMZNv8g1irTHBmEH","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np = \"attavo/cli.py\"\ns = open(p).read()\nold = '''budget. [checks] is optional; a tenant that declares none is not\nrefused. It writes the next build-NN.json'''\nnew = '''budget. [checks] is optional; a tenant that declares none is not\nrefused. Before the adapter is invoked it asks whether this machine can\nrun the checks -- of [checks].probe, run once inside [checks].probe_timeout_s\n(exit 0 yes; anything else, or the bound, an environment refusal), or,\nfor a tenant that declares no probe, by running [checks].command whole\n(exit 2 no) -- and says both the question and the answer in the feed\n(issue #212). The adapter is given ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND, `attavo test N`,\nand ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S when [tests].call_timeout_s is declared; it\nis not given the tenant's checks. It writes the next build-NN.json'''\nassert old in s\ns = s.replace(old, new, 1)\nold2 = '''verify refuses (exit 1) unless the item's latest build record has'''\nnew2 = '''test [N] runs the tests [tests].select names for every path the item has\nchanged since it left the default branch (refs/remotes/origin/HEAD),\ncommitted or not and untracked included, paths.records aside, through\n[tests].run. It prints how many were selected (or that none was, and runs\nnothing), exits as the run does, and, when [tests].call_timeout_s is\ndeclared and the run outlasts it, ends the run and everything it started\nand exits 124. It exits 2 when it cannot name the changes or the selector\nfails. It is the one test command an executor is given (issue #212).\n\nverify refuses (exit 1) unless the item's latest build record has'''\nassert old2 in s\ns = s.replace(old2, new2, 1)\nopen(p, \"w\").write(s)\n\n# adapters README\np = \"adapters/README.md\"\ns = open(p).read()\nold = [l for l in s.splitlines() if l.startswith(\"- `ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND`\")][0]\nnew = (\"- `ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND` — build only: the one test command the executor is given, `attavo test <N>` (issue #212). It runs the tests the tenant's `[tests].select` names for every path the item has changed since it left the default branch, committed or not, through `[tests].run`, and exits as the run does. An adapter tells the executor to run it while working, and not to run the whole test suite or any whole-tree check: the tenant's `[checks].command` is run at the gate after every commit, and a command the executor is named is a command the executor runs (#194's build-01 waited 590 s on the suite inside the executor). The tenant's checks command is not part of the contract.\\n\"\n       \"- `ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S` — build only, set with `ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND` when the tenant declares `[tests].call_timeout_s`: the seconds one `attavo test` run is given before it is ended and exits 124. An adapter says so in the same sentence; absent, it says nothing about a bound.\")\ns = s.replace(old, new)\nopen(p, \"w\").write(s)\n\np = \"adapters/claude-code/README.md\"\ns = open(p).read()\ni = s.index(\"## The tenant's checks\")\nj = s.index(\"## The sandbox is the boundary\")\ns = s[:i] + '''## The tenant's tests\n\n`attavo build` runs the tenant's gates after each commit and feeds a\nfailure back on the next iteration — the executor is not the runner of the\ntenant's checks, and is not told what they are. When `ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND`\nis set (`../README.md`), the instruction gives it: \"to run tests while you\nwork, run `<command>`: it runs the tests selected for the files you have\nchanged and stops at `<N>` s. Do not run the whole test suite or any\nwhole-tree check yourself: after you commit, the gates are run for you and\nany failure is returned to you on the next iteration.\" The \"stops at\" clause\nis present only when `ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S` is set. When\n`ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND` is unset, the instruction says nothing about tests.\n\n''' + s[j:]\nopen(p, \"w\").write(s)\nEOF\ngit diff adapters/README.md | head -20; sed -n 40,70p adapters/codex/README.md; grep -n \"instruction\" adapters/codex/README.md | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":963,"cache_read_input_tokens":108645,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":963},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8327c9db-455b-4a76-8736-ba592c30dfef","uuid":"5d587c31-ff6b-4c2e-9a69-db5b07bce585","timestamp":"2026-09-21T01:46:57.411Z","request_id":"req_011CfFjvuzgstnZnFuzdkrLk","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01TYDQtfnMZNv8g1irTHBmEH":{"command":"cd /Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-212 && python3 - <<'EOF'\np = \"attavo/cli.py\"\ns = open(p).read()\nold = '''budget. [checks] is optional; a tenant that declares none is not\nrefused. It writes the next build-NN.json'''\nnew = '''budget. [checks] is optional; a tenant that declares none is not\nrefused. Before the adapter is invoked it asks whether this machine can\nrun the checks -- of [checks].probe, run once inside [checks].probe_timeout_s\n(exit 0 yes; anything else, or the bound, an environment refusal), or,\nfor a tenant that declares no probe, by running [checks].command whole\n(exit 2 no) -- and says both the question and the answer in the feed\n(issue #212). The adapter is given ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND, `attavo test N`,\nand ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S when [tests].call_timeout_s is declared; it\nis not given the tenant's checks. It writes the next build-NN.json'''\nassert old in s\ns = s.replace(old, new, 1)\nold2 = '''verify refuses (exit 1) unless the item's latest build record has'''\nnew2 = '''test [N] runs the tests [tests].select