he sandbox is the boundary\")\ns = s[:i] + '''## The tenant's tests\n\n`attavo build` runs the tenant's gates after each commit and feeds a\nfailure back on the next iteration — the executor is not the runner of the\ntenant's checks, and is not told what they are. When `ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND`\nis set (`../README.md`), the instruction gives it: \"to run tests while you\nwork, run `<command>`: it runs the tests selected for the files you have\nchanged and stops at `<N>` s. Do not run the whole test suite or any\nwhole-tree check yourself: after you commit, the gates are run for you and\nany failure is returned to you on the next iteration.\" The \"stops at\" clause\nis present only when `ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S` is set. When\n`ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND` is unset, the instruction says nothing about tests.\n\n''' + s[j:]\nopen(p, \"w\").write(s)\nEOF\ngit diff adapters/README.md | head -20; sed -n 40,70p adapters/codex/README.md; grep -n \"instruction\" adapters/codex/README.md | head"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01TYDQtfnMZNv8g1irTHBmEH":{"cwd":"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-212"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TYDQtfnMZNv8g1irTHBmEH","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/adapters/README.md b/adapters/README.md\nindex bf06683..7148371 100644\n--- a/adapters/README.md\n+++ b/adapters/README.md\n@@ -13,7 +13,8 @@ the tenant's `attavo/adapters/`, then under this product's `adapters/`.\n - `ATTAVO_ITERATION` — the 1-based attempt number within this `attavo build` invocation.\n - `ATTAVO_FEEDBACK` — a file holding the previous iteration's failing criteria, test output, and checks output; empty on the first iteration.\n - `ATTAVO_ADAPTER_CONFIG` — the tenant manifest's `[executor.<adapter-name>]` table, serialized as JSON (`{}` when the tenant declared none). The product does not know what an adapter's settings mean; each adapter documents its own keys on its own `README.md`. **Never put a secret in this table** — it is copied verbatim into `build-NN.json` as `adapter_config`, and a record is not where secrets live.\n-- `ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND` — the tenant's `[checks].command`, unset when the tenant declared no `[checks]` table. The product does not know what it checks; the tenant does. An adapter should tell the executor it is part of done when set, and say nothing about checks when it is not.\n+- `ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND` — build only: the one test command the executor is given, `attavo test <N>` (issue #212). It runs the tests the tenant's `[tests].select` names for every path the item has changed since it left the default branch, committed or not, through `[tests].run`, and exits as the run does. An adapter tells the executor to run it while working, and not to run the whole test suite or any whole-tree check: the tenant's `[checks].command` is run at the gate after every commit, and a command the executor is named is a command the executor runs (#194's build-01 waited 590 s on the suite inside the executor). The tenant's checks command is not part of the contract.\n+- `ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S` — build only, set with `ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND` when the tenant declares `[tests].call_timeout_s`: the seconds one `attavo test` run is given before it is ended and exits 124. An adapter says so in the same sentence; absent, it says nothing about a bound.\n - `ATTAVO_STAGE` — `\"build\"`, `\"verify\"`, or `\"counsel\"` (issue #100), which invocation this is. An adapter that supports every stage branches on it; one that only builds may ignore it.\n - `ATTAVO_EVENTS` — build and verify only: a file path an adapter may append events to while it runs (issue #26). Absent on a stage that does not set it (counsel does not); an adapter that never checks for it breaks nothing.\n - `ATTAVO_DIFF` — verify only: a file holding the diff since the build's approval.\n- `--json` prints one JSON object per stdout line (JSONL): `thread.started`,\n  `turn.started`, `item.*`, and a terminal `turn.completed` (carrying\n  `usage`) or `turn.failed`. codex's own exit code is 1 on `turn.failed`,\n  0 on `turn.completed` -- read directly, so this adapter reads the\n  terminal event for the reason, not for the verdict.\n- `--output-schema <FILE>` plus `--output-last-message <FILE>` writes the\n  final response as one JSON object once the turn completes -- this is\n  where `findings`/`tests_named` (verify) or `status`/`question` (build)\n  come from.\n\n## Events (issue #138)\n\nWith `ATTAVO_EVENTS` set, each `item.completed` line on the `--json`\nstream maps to `../README.md`'s shared `{at, kind, text}` shape: an\n`agent_message` item's own text to `message` (confirmed live, issue\n#41 -- `conformance.json`'s own `\"done\"` situation is this exact\nspecimen), a `command_execution` item's `command` to `tool_call` and,\nonce present, its `aggregated_output` to `tool_result` (both the\ncommand's and the output's own first line only, capped at 400\ncharacters) -- `command` and `aggregated_output` are confirmed, by\ntenant zero's own verify logs on `attavo/code-factory` since #649:\nevery `command_execution` item there carries exactly the keys\n`aggregated_output`, `command`, `exit_code`, `id`, `status`, `type`,\nthe same shape `tests/test_adapter_codex.py`'s own recorded fixture\nexercises this mapping through. Every other item\ntype, and every non-`item.completed` line, maps to nothing. Read from\nthe same `events` list `invoke()` already parses for the report line's\nown token count, whether from a live run or a canned\n`ATTAVO_ADAPTER_RESPONSE_FILE` -- codex's own invocation is not a\nstream read as it happens the way claude-code's is (issue #26): the\nevents land in `ATTAVO_EVENTS` once the whole call returns, not before.\n33:instruction to plain `codex exec -` on stdin (`-p` is codex's\n72:## The sandbox, not just the instruction\n74:`verify`'s instruction says \"make no edits, write no files, commit\n77:this adapter trusting the instruction alone. Not a tenant-configurable\n82:- `ATTAVO_ADAPTER_DRY_RUN` prints `{\"argv\", \"instruction\", \"schema\"}`\n83:  instead of running. `argv` never carries the instruction -- it goes in\n101:this adapter re-invokes `codex exec` once more (the same reinstruction\n102:text appended to the instruction) before ever reporting a halt. A second","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8327c9db-455b-4a76-8736-ba592c30dfef","uuid":"da91b1ac-bd6d-431f-a65e-eeb690fe66f3","timestamp":"2026-09-21T01:46:57.549Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"diff --git a/adapters/README.md b/adapters/README.md\nindex bf06683..7148371 100644\n--- a/adapters/README.md\n+++ b/adapters/README.md\n@@ -13,7 +13,8 @@ the tenant's `attavo/adapters/`, then under this product's `adapters/`.\n - `ATTAVO_ITERATION` — the 1-based attempt number within this `attavo build` invocation.\n - `ATTAVO_FEEDBACK` — a file holding the previous iteration's failing criteria, test output, and checks output; empty on the first iteration.\n - `ATTAVO_ADAPTER_CONFIG` — the tenant manifest's `[executor.<adapter-name>]` table, serialized as JSON (`{}` when the 